# Git-level line-ending normalization (last-resort CRLF defence; the IDE .editorconfig
# is the first layer). Ensures Java and other text sources are stored and checked out
# with LF regardless of the developer's OS or core.autocrlf setting.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.java   text eol=lf
*.xml    text eol=lf
*.yml    text eol=lf
*.yaml   text eol=lf
*.json   text eol=lf
*.sh     text eol=lf
*.properties text eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts keep CRLF.
*.cmd    text eol=crlf
*.bat    text eol=crlf

# Binaries: never normalize.
*.jar    binary
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.gif    binary
*.p12    binary
*.jks    binary

# Flyway migrations are checksummed artifacts, not ordinary source: Core reports a Java
# migration's checksum from DatabaseMigration.JavaMigrationChecksums and Flyway derives a SQL
# migration's from the file itself, both validated against the value stored when the migration
# ran. -text keeps git from rewriting a single byte of them, so no checkout, renormalisation or
# core.autocrlf setting can ever disturb a shipped migration. Spotless and Checkstyle skip the
# same paths - see the plugin excludes in pom.xml.
src/main/java/db/migration/**       -text
src/main/resources/db/migration/**  -text

# Generated data artifacts: files a generator writes in full, never a human. Marking them
# generated collapses them behind a click in a pull request and drops them from the repository's
# language statistics. They stay diffable, which matters: the reproducibility gate in
# .github/workflows/build_pr.yml prints the drift when a regeneration disagrees with the committed
# bytes, and that output is only useful if git will still render it.
#
# The entry condition is that something regenerates the file and CI proves it. identity-tables.json
# qualifies: `Generated artifacts` rebuilds it from the inputs on every pull request and fails on a
# single differing byte, so nobody has to read it to trust it.
#
# identity-key-vectors.json is deliberately NOT listed. It looks like bulk data and it is, but no
# generator produces it and no job checks it, so reading the diff is the only thing standing between
# a silently edited expectation and a green run. Collapsing it would remove that guard while looking
# like housekeeping.
src/main/resources/cbom/identity-tables.json         linguist-generated=true

# Vendored upstream snapshots feeding the generator, reviewed at the version they were taken
# from, not hunk by hunk. cryptography-defs.schema.json is byte-identical to the copy shipped
# in org.cyclonedx:cyclonedx-core-java:13.2.0 apart from a trailing newline.
src/main/cbom/identity/cryptography-defs.json        linguist-generated=true
src/main/cbom/identity/cryptography-defs.schema.json linguist-generated=true

# oid-strand.json is deliberately NOT marked: it is a ratified local decision set carrying
# per-arc rationale, and its diff IS the review material.
